      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for these. They're a good start, but I just ran them through the internal tracker and the score came back really low—it basically flagged that we're missing almost all of our core theme keywords. \n\nI know I said not to overdo it, but we really need to make sure the questions are clearly hitting those specific pillars so the system recognizes them. Can you revise these 5 questions so they feel a bit more aligned with our specific terminology? \n\nJust a reminder: please don't make them weird or just jam the words in there for the sake of the score. I still need them to be professional, high-level behavioral questions that actually work in a real interview. Can you try again to get that score up without making them sound like nonsense?",
